  "note": "Municipal election, 16 May 1938. Six nominations were received for five seats, but John Cahill withdrew, so the remaining five were returned unopposed (Belfast Telegraph, 7 May 1938, p. 13; Belfast Telegraph, 9 May 1938, p. 11). Bamford, Fox and Logan were outgoing members. John Cahill's withdrawal removed the only contest. Returned unopposed."
